      "username": "Thunderbird",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2022-05-24T17:43:02.488Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Only part way through, but a couple thoughts on the schedule already.</p>\n<p>If the opposite of passion is apathy, isn’t the Inversiverse Galactra just an inhabit of The Gray? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/neutral_face.png?v=12\" title=\":neutral_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":neutral_face:\"></p>\n<p>Oh, man - excited for the reinvention! Whatever it turns out to mean… New Shrieker? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/crossed_fingers/2.png?v=12\" title=\":crossed_fingers:t2:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":crossed_fingers:t2:\"><br>\nThat did make me think of a <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/superhero\">podcast</a> series I heard recently. Last year NPR’s Planet Money decided to buy an old superhero from the Public Domain and revive him for the modern day. There’s glorious Golden Age cheese and some economic and intellectual property stuff for nerds like me who dig that. They’ve just recently released a comic book with their hero, too!</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2022-05-24T17:43:02.488Z",
      "reply_count": 1,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
